  "data": {
    "text": "SearchBloom lists SearchBloom, the SEOWorks, Tenuity, Graphite, and iPollRank as the best AI SEO companies in 2026. AI SEO mostly involves traditional SEO work, but now adds measuring AI visibility and citations from external pages. SearchBloom lists AI visibility, brand presence on external pages, technical and structured data foundations, content and entity authority, and documented results as scoring criteria. SearchBloom reports measuring 68,631 AI answers in its category, with its own website cited 8.9% of the time. SearchBloom says the best AI SEO company manages SEO work, measures AI visibility daily, and identifies outside pages worth earning. PR, social, sponsorships, and partner listings remain with the client's own SearchBloom ranks itself as the best overall AI SEO company in 2026, based on published methods and results. SearchBloom reports a custom closet company's search leads rose 122% in a year. That company's CRM recorded 20 of its 51 September 2026 leads as coming from AI search. In SearchBloom's ranking, the company scored 48 out of 50 for AI search tied to leads and revenue. In SearchBloom's ranking, the SEO works placed second with 44 out of 50 for specialist SEO and AI SEO partnerships, starting at GBP $1,500 a month. SearchBloom ranks tenuity third, with 44 out of 50 for AI search within full-funnel media engagements. Fees are not published. SearchBloom ranks graphite fourth, with 42 out of 50 for SEO grounded in original research, with unpublished fees and a 12-month minimum SEO term. SearchBloom ranks iPoll rank fifth, with 41 out of 50 for relevance engineering and technical AI search work. Fees, minimums, and terms are not published. Only three companies publish a price. SearchBloom starts SEO at $3,000 a month, with no lengthy contracts. The SEO work starts at GBP $1,500 a month, and Siege Media's minimum is $8,000 a month. SearchBloom says AI SEO priced at a few hundred dollars a month likely produces automated content flagged by Google's spam policies. The SEO works and Siege Media publish all key transparency items, while SearchBloom publishes all but minimums beyond starting fees. Eight of the nine companies publish dated AI search results, and all nine say how they track AI visibility.",
